nora: quick flag - my docs PR updating the retry guidance is blocked. the SDK snippet assumes the server's Retry-After header is in seconds, but runtime seems to be emitting milliseconds for some proxy responses. preview failed and i need a runtime/SDK call before the docs cut.

docs-ci-bot: preview failed - rendering error in /docs/guides/retries.md line 27. full logs: https://ci.internal/reports/2026504321

sam: ah, yes. we rolled a proxy change that preserves upstream Retry-After values; some backends send it in ms (internal infra) while public endpoints historically use seconds. didn't intend to change public contract. i'll confirm which routes are affected and link the commit.

devon: SDK currently does `const wait = parseInt(resp.headers['retry-after'], 10) * 1000` (always treats as seconds). that breaks when header is already ms. i've got a follow-up SDK PR draft to normalize, but it won't land before the cut.

chen: for docs, two safe paths: (A) make the example robust (show parsing that tolerates seconds or ms and documents both cases), or (B) call out the ambiguity and mark the page as "implementation-dependent". with release window ~18h i'd prefer (A) so copy-paste examples behave.

nora: agreed - i'll add a small snippet demonstrating a tolerant parser and a short note explaining the runtime variance across proxies. question for reviewers: is it ok to document a tolerant approach rather than asserting a single canonical unit?

sam: yes, document tolerant parsing. i'll also open a runtime issue to either normalize Retry-After to seconds at the edge or add a header flag. linking commit: https://git.internal/redwood/runtime/commit/f8b3c1 and issue: https://git.internal/redwood/runtime/issues/910

devon: good plan. i'll fast-track the SDK helper `parseRetryAfter(header)` after the release. until then examples should use a defensive approach. example i suggest:

```
// tolerant Retry-After parsing
function parseRetryAfter(hdr) {
  if (!hdr) return 0;
  const n = Number(hdr);
  if (Number.isNaN(n)) return 0;
  // if value looks large (> 10k) treat as ms, otherwise seconds
  return n > 10000 ? Math.ceil(n / 1000) : Math.ceil(n);
}

const retry = parseRetryAfter(resp.headers['retry-after']);
setTimeout(retryHandler, retry * 1000);
```

small comment: 10k threshold is heuristic — document that.

chen: add a short footnote recommending server-side normalization if possible and warn about clock skew/precision when using ms. also mention the SDK helper will land later and link the follow-up.

nora: updated PR with tolerant snippet + note and added links to runtime issue and SDK follow-up: https://git.internal/redwood/docs/pull/5489

docs-ci-bot: preview queued (job 10421). link: https://ci.internal/preview/10421

docs-ci-bot: preview succeeded - rendering & linkcheck passed. artifacts: https://ci.internal/preview/10421/artifacts

sam: quick review: wording looks good and doesn't overpromise. i'll own the runtime follow-up to pick a single unit for public endpoints.

devon: LGTM from docs perspective. i'll open the SDK PR and link it to the runtime issue.

nora: thanks all. i'll merge after a short hold and file a cross-team follow-up to align public contract vs internal proxies. merging plan: merge now, watch errors for 20m, then close runtime/sdk issues when ready. :shipit:
